side. Both 24.b3?? and 25.a4?? left the e1-rook unprotected on the open file, giving you the chance for an immediate knockout. You missed it with 24...Bg7?? and 25...f5??, but when White erred again with 27.Bxf4??, you finally unleashed 27...Nf3+!. This move delivered a fork against the king and rook while creating a discovered attack down the e-file, winning the exchange on e1.","line":"27.Bxf4 Nf3+ 28.gxf3 Rxe1"}],"turning_point":"White's 27.Bxf4?? allowed 27...Nf3+!, where the knight fork and discovered attack down the open e-file won decisive material.","focus":"Look for discovered attacks along open files when an opponent leaves a major piece undefended, such as the missed 24...Nf3+.","model":"google/gemini-3.7-flash","v":2,"cost":0.004119,"at":1793768023398}}
